    {'para': '**92. Verbs. Present Indicative active. Unaccented ⟨a⟩-class.** A number of roots conjugated in this class have medial short ⟨a⟩. Inasmuch as “⟨a⟩ is its own *guṇa*”, these roots merely add an ⟨a⟩ to form the present-stem; e.g., ⟨vad⟩, present-stem ⟨vada⟩. The final ⟨a⟩ of the stem is lengthened in the three first persons.'},
